ocstring 'An imaginary quadratic field is totally complex') states it: a number field containing an algebraic integer theta with minpoly Z theta = X\^2 - d and d \< 0, in particular Q(sqrt d), is totally complex. It rests on NumberField.isTotallyComplex\_of\_sq\_ratCast\_of\_neg (TauCeti.NumberTheory.NumberField.InfinitePlace.Basic): any field with x\^2 = r for a negative rational r is totally complex, which covers every presentation of an imaginary quadratic field. Non-vacuous: Tau Ceti applies it to Q(i), Q(sqrt -5) and Q(sqrt -21). (3) 'The plots are produced using SageMath ...': provenance and display. The audit (N4) proposed 'To be formalised' with 'no lemma states it'; it missed the Tau Ceti lemma, so the category is Formalised in Tau Ceti (with Mathlib). No text error. Review: the six declarations exist at the pins in the modules recorded, with the meanings stated; axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.

